meta {
  name: POST Ingest Signal (Paper BUY)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/webhook/{{paperWebhookToken}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "comment": "paper-secret-1",
    "type": "ORDER_SIGNAL",
    "symbol": "SBIN",
    "action": "BUY",
    "quantity": 12,
    "order_type": "LIMIT"
  }
}

tests {
  test("Status 202 queued (not filled yet)", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(202);
    expect(res.getBody().queued).to.equal(true);
  });
}

docs {
  Paper-destination webhooks require this typed payload — `type: "ORDER_SIGNAL"`
  places/closes an order, `type: "PRICE_UPDATE"` marks a price (see
  ingest-price-update.bru). `comment` is checked against the webhook's
  `required_comment` — same field name and mechanism as live trading. Field is
  `quantity`, not `lot`.
  
  `order_type`, if present, must match the webhook's configured
  `default_order_type` (unset here, so LIMIT — see Webhooks → create-webhook
  Paper) or the request is rejected; the actual order type used for the fill
  always comes from that webhook config, same as the legacy shape.
  
  `price` is required in v1 (no market data feed) — omitting it fills with a
  REJECTED order, visible via GET .../orders (see Failure Modes → Paper Trading).
  
  Ingest always returns 202 immediately; the fill happens async in the queue
  worker. Check Paper Trading → positions / orders / pnl after this to see the
  outcome (give it ~1s).
}
